# aurora.local / packages/privacy/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/privacy/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/privacy/pins.env to adopt.
#
# Every pin below is curated and human-reviewed.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# adguard/adguardhome — latest stable is v0.107.78 (the v0.108 line is
# still in beta, `-b.xx` pre-releases only — deliberately avoided). This
# release is a security release (path traversal, JIGGLE attack mitigation,
# stricter DoH/DNSCrypt upstream validation, Go updated for CVEs fixed in
# Go 1.26.5) — a good reason to move onto it rather than sit on an older
# 0.107.7x. Confirmed `:latest` currently resolves to the exact same
# digest as v0.107.78, so this is not a downgrade from what a fresh pull
# would get today. Multi-arch: linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v6,
# linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64, linux/ppc64le — confirmed via `docker buildx
# imagetools inspect`; covers both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64).
# Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_ADGUARD=adguard/adguardhome:v0.107.78@sha256:1ea34eafe5dc691007946e8eaab7bf46b0de9412f39213d8c06e48b53bf9a6c5

# qmcgaw/gluetun — latest confirmed stable release is v3.41.1 (published
# 2026-02-11). Note: the maintainer has signalled v3.42.0 is coming, and
# the project's GitHub org is mid-migration to github.com/passteque/gluetun
# (the qmcgaw/gluetun *image name* is explicitly stated to stay the same
# through the move, so this pin is not at risk from the rename). No v3.42
# tag was confirmed to exist at the time of this check — worth a re-check
# before long, since a VPN client is exactly the kind of thing you don't
# want stale if a CVE lands. `:latest` currently resolves to a different,
# newer digest than v3.41.1, which likely means an unreleased/edge build
# rather than a missed stable tag — do not chase `:latest` here. Multi-
# arch: linux/amd64, linux/386, linux/arm64, linux/arm/v6, linux/arm/v7,
# linux/ppc64le — confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools inspect`; covers
# both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64). Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_GLUETUN=qmcgaw/gluetun:v3.41.1@sha256:1a5bf4b4820a879cdf8d93d7ef0d2d963af56670c9ebff8981860b6804ebc8ab
